# evidence-for: US-010, FR-039, FR-029, FR-043, AC-039, GI-004, GI-007, OT-043
#
# GRIND cycle 15. The lead asked for every remaining "would", "only", "different" and "each one"
# clause in this casting's two files to be mutation-measured before it was left standing. Nine
# blocks; the three defects D-154, D-155 and D-156 have their own logs.
#
# Two clauses did not survive and are corrected in the same commit.
#
# conftest.py said that because a module-level assignment freezes at import, "for those five,
# subprocess is the only honest way to drive the script at all". Block [1] measures both halves:
# the freeze is real - an imported drift.py keeps the cwd it was imported under - but a second
# exec_module re-binds it, and runpy.run_path drives drift.py check to a real status and exit code
# inside this process. The paragraph now says what an in-process run of those five costs (a fresh
# execution per scenario, and no process boundary) rather than calling it impossible. Block [2]
# measures the other half of the same paragraph, that the two scripts reading argv inside main can
# be driven by import + main().
#
# test_harness.py's GIT_ENV comment was wrong in the same way D-156 was. Block [7]: neither a
# global status.relativePaths nor an alias shadowing ls-files changes any of the three queries
# this module runs - all three digests are equal across all three configurations. The guard stays,
# because it costs nothing and the argument for it was never the two examples; the examples do
# not.
#
# The other seven held as written:
#
#   [3] conftest FIXTURE_COMMITS: "both of those builds run in one process, on one host, in one
#       zone, and agree with or without the offset" - two offset-stripped builds, one HEAD.
#   [4] conftest build_fixture_repo: a TZ set with os.environ and time.tzset "never reaches the
#       child at all" - the parent reads +1400 while git dates the commit at the host's offset.
#   [5] conftest _BASE_ENV_KEYS: a shell WEBSTER_ var "would otherwise silently change what the
#       script under test sees" - with the key list widened to all of os.environ, drift.py read
#       the shell's WEBSTER_DOCS instead of its own default.
#   [6] conftest fixture_repo: "a shared copy would make one test's mutation another test's
#       premise" - one consumer's append is visible to the next and leaves the tree dirty.
#   [8] conftest: "line numbers appear below only for files outside this change's writable
#       surface" - what remains points at plugins/forge, which GI-007 freezes, plus
#       src/app/main.py:15, the anchor string the fixture plants rather than a citation.
#   [9] test_harness: FR-039 named by all seven test modules at c3efe37 and FR-029, FR-030,
#       FR-042 and FR-043 by none.
#
# Two clauses in these files assert nothing measurable and were left alone rather than hedged:
# conftest's "seven near-identical wrappers would drift apart" and test_harness's "a recursive
# glob would have waved the whole tree through". Both are design rationale about a shape that was
# not built, not claims about behaviour this suite can put a command behind.

